From 5608af7484b2eb7d68ad9590116f52d063ec7c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 11:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: starfive: fix PineTab-V audio jack routing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PineTab-V headset connector pulls HP_DET low when a plug is inserted,
but the Device Tree currently describes it as active high.  This reverses
jack availability in userspace: inserting headphones selects the speakers
and removing them leaves the headphone route selected.

GPIO13 is not a microphone insertion switch.  The schematic shows
HEADSET_MIC_DET_GPIO13 strapped high through R215 and decoupled by C324,
with no connection to the headset socket.  Do not expose it as a dynamic
microphone jack detector.  Use the headset insertion event for both the
headphone and headset-microphone UCM routes instead.

Keep pin switches only for endpoints that userspace must route
explicitly.  The Headphones DAPM pin is owned by the physical jack GPIO
and must not also be driven by a UCM pin switch, which otherwise races
with jack events.

Name the card after the board and codec, and expose independent switches
for the internal microphone, headset microphone and internal speakers.

Link: https://files.pine64.org/doc/PineTab/PineTab-V_Schematic_Ver2-20240730.pdf
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 .../boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi   | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi
@@ -229,6 +229,9 @@
-		simple-audio-card,name = "PineTab-V";
+		simple-audio-card,name = "PineTab-V ES8316 Audio";
 		simple-audio-card,aux-devs = <&speaker_amp>;
-		simple-audio-card,hp-det-gpios = <&sysgpio 36 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		simple-audio-card,hp-det-gpios = <&sysgpio 36 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		simple-audio-card,pin-switches =
+			"Internal Microphone", "Headset Microphone",
+			"Internal Speakers";
 		simple-audio-card,widgets =
 			"Microphone", "Internal Microphone",
 			"Microphone", "Headset Microphone",
-- 
